mbies universe for a premium fee of 5  000 zombie bucks  you can increase your gun's power and  ammo capacity while obtaining a sweet  but cursed  paint job using the powers of element  115 the pack-a-punch machine not only  kicks your gun into overdrive but can  change some of its attributes  for example in some games like black ops  1 you can change the fire rate of the  m16 from a 3 round burst to full  auto with noob tubes and like i  mentioned it can pack a single handgun  firing regular bullets  to a dual wielding menace that fires  grenade rounds  not so much anymore but he used to  bottom line a zombie's map without a  pack of punch machine  is simply incomplete  with every annual release of call of  duty we'd see the same setup  campaign and online multiplayer the  bread and butter of call of duty games  but outside of the dlc multiplayer maps  there wasn't much else in terms of  variety  enter zombies mode it was a great way to  break up those long gaming nights  after some sweaty matches of multiplayer  you can swap over to zombies and take  out your kd frustrations on the undead  my friends and i would go back and forth  between game modes until someone would  finally call alright last one for me  it was only then when i realized it was  actually 4 a.m  oh where does the time go  troy loves to hide secrets in zombies  mode and we love to find them  everything from music to intel nearly  every map is brimming with secrets  why are they gonna put a music easter  egg in every map now  who else goes around every new map and  mashing the interact button like it's  resident evil  sniffing around and hoping to unlock  something before your friends do  sometimes they were just for fun but  other times these secrets would reveal  little parts of the greater story  everything was always so shrouded in  mystery and we'd lived for it  nowadays even with a more streamlined  story intel can be found all over the  place  you get radio conversations and side  stories about your team and their  findings  best of all you can re-listen to them  anytime  speaking of stories it's mind-blowing to  think that  zombies started out as a simple survival  mode with absolutely no story  when world at war launched in 2008 the  vanilla release didn't even have voices  for your character  soon enough new maps characters and the  beginning of a grand story arc formed  around this little game mode  if you've played zombies for a while you  know how tangled the tales could get  i myself didn't play black ops 3 so when  i picked it back up with black ops 4  i was like what the [ __ ] happened here i  was pretty confused but  i wasn't alone there are so many  explainer videos on youtube that it  makes my head spin  people ate this stuff up and that's  because treyarch does  not skimp out when it comes to  storytelling some might even say they go  overboard in this department  but it doesn't matter because even if  you don't follow the story  the core gameplay of zombies will always  shine through  currently we're in a place where the  zombie story is a little more at ease  but it's slowly building to something  bigger i can feel it  [Music]  ah perks cracking a cold one to unlock a  superpower  just can't be beat over the years there  have been several perk machines  each offering a fun and unique way to  turn you into a zombie killing machine  there are the classic perks like  juggernog and speed cola and more were  introduced that were helpful  in unexpected ways perks like death  perception that lets you see  enemies through walls or electric bursts  which zaps enemies around you while you  reload  in some maps you were limited to only  four  but today you can have as many as you  want and they can each be leveled up  multiple times for other effects some of  these effects are actually old perks you  may remember  while perks are a necessity for higher  rounds of zombies they're also just sort  of fun to collect  so buy them all and watch as your player  becomes an absolute  tank i already mentioned secrets but  this  is the big stuff easter eggs and call of  duty are the crown jewel of the entire  mode  it's puzzle solving storytelling boss  fighting and dumb luck  rolled all into one it's also the  fastest way to lose track of time  hours will go by as you try to solve  these especially if you're on your own  or without a guide  these easter eggs can push your zombie  survival skills to their limits  but the payoff is always worth it even  if you don't pay attention to the story  these are what help elevate zombies from  a survival mode to the thrilling and  involved story that it is today  personally speaking i was already in  love with the core mode from day one  but when they started adding all these  easter eggs in i knew the mode was here  to stay  eventually the series would feature  detailed stories in the style of  animated stills  but for some of the bigger moments  treyarch produced full cinematics that  were  unforgettable  now more than ever call of duty zombies  can't be stopped  its story is vast and its gameplay is as  addictive as ever  there's also a nice flow of content with  new maps and wonder weapons and stories  added in every season  from the beginning people have wanted  more and more zombies  even begging for a dedicated zombies  game that would stand alone from the  black  ops titles only time will tell if we  ever see that until then  share your love for zombies in the  comments and drop a like if you enjoyed  this list  alright that'll do it for me i'm gonna  go play some zombies  you
 

